I replied on the two issues I worked on this session and skipped the rest, because I had nothing new to say on them.

• #1183 (fixed, closed): In the REPL, /provider custom (with or without a base URL) and /provider github when the session has a base URL are now refused and nothing is changed. This is the same rule startup has used since #1175. The refusal tells the user to restart with --provider … --model <id>. A test runs through every provider name, with and without a base URL, and checks exactly which ones are refused. Other tests check the full refusal text and that the suggested restart command parses. My comment says the tests run the real switch code but I didn't try it in a live REPL.
• #1184 (progress, kept open): First step landed. Every config file yoyo loads is now parsed with the toml crate before anything runs. Invalid TOML stops yoyo with the file, line and column, the bad line, and exit 2. The comment names the three behaviour changes:
  • model = m1 used to run as m1; it is now refused.
  • Duplicate keys used to keep the last value silently; they are now refused.
  • The inspection commands (config show/get, doctor and others) now refuse invalid TOML instead of only warning.

  Still to do: move the readers onto typed structs, write through toml_edit, and delete the hand parser and its tests once their cases are moved.
